    "type": "question",
    "label": "17",
    "prompt": "First introduce a pronumeral and then solve the equation.\n\nSubtracting 10 from 6 times a number gives the same result as multiplying the number by 7 and adding 6. What is the number?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "The number is $-16$.",
      "worked": "Let $x$ be the number.\n$$\\begin{align*}6x-10&=7x+6\\\\-10&=x+6\\\\-16&=x\\\\x&=-16\\end{align*}$$\nCheck: $6(-16)-10=-106$ and $7(-16)+6=-106$.\n\nThe number is $-16$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 52
